DYATLOV PASS — an original red paper-cut documentary made with the Lemo-Opuscar toolkit
=======================================================================================

Story, pictures, music and narration script are original works for this film.
Historical facts follow the Wikipedia article "Dyatlov Pass incident",
Gaume & Puzrin, "A mechanism for the Dyatlov Pass incident",
Communications Earth & Environment 2, 10 (2021), and 2020 Russian prosecutor
general coverage (Kuryakov). Tone: documentary and respectful — no gore, no monsters.

Engine
- Lemo-Opuscar core tools (rendering, tts, sampler, pluck, sfx, mux): MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 LemoLab — https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar
- Papercut-red paper-cut engine (paper.js, motifs.js, rig.js, light.js, hud.js) adapted from the
  styles/papercut-red demo (MIT, LemoLab); all scene code (story.js, hikers.js, world.js, scenes.js, main.js)
  is original for this film.

Fonts (in fonts/)
- Fraunces — SIL Open Font License 1.1, Undercase Type / The Fraunces Project Contributors.

Narration
- Kokoro TTS v1.0 (kokoro-v1.0.onnx), voice am_michael — Apache-2.0, hexgrad.
- Line-by-line verification: whisper base.en (OpenAI, MIT) via faster-whisper.

Sound samples (via core/audio/sampler.py)
- VCSL (Versilian Community Sample Library) — CC0 1.0.
- Karoryfer Samples instruments (flute, woodblock, world percussion) — CC0 1.0.
- Pipa is physically modelled (core/audio/pluck.py); zheng uses dan_tranh samples; gong and frame drum
  from CC0 sample sets.

All audio is mixed offline with numpy/scipy; loudness conformed at mux (−14 LUFS).
